                                       '<p>Introducing a 20 mm deep biomechanical heel cup produced an immediate, '
                                       'statistically significant redistribution of plantar loads. Contact surface '
                                       'area around the rearfoot expanded by 64%, spreading vertical impact forces '
                                       'across the lateral and posterior heel walls. Peak subcalcaneal contact '
                                       'pressures plummeted to <strong>264 ± 18 kPa</strong>—a dramatic 42.3% '
